MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo Show 5 feels like a useful addition to my Fire TV setup because its screen offers something beyond my voice remote, especially if it can display my cameras.",
    "The newer Echo Dot fits my interest in convenient home control through Alexa, although I would choose the Echo Show's screen this time."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The previous-generation Fire TV Stick repeats a function I already have through my 4K stick and Fire TV television, without giving me a clear reason to replace either.",
    "The memory cards have a possible connection to my cameras, but I have neither a confirmed storage need nor confirmed compatibility. The tablet, earbuds, USB hub, and carrying case address needs I have not expressed."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying Fire TV devices seems to have been taken as interest in almost any Amazon device, even older products that add little to my setup.",
    "My electronics purchases seem to have been treated as a reason to suggest general accessories, although I usually need a specific purpose before buying them."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What I already own matters: a useful addition should offer a new capability rather than repeat my existing television and streaming functions.",
    "My recent camera and television purchases make home viewing and monitoring more relevant than portable entertainment or generic accessories, but any camera-related addition still needs to work with my equipment."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions recognize my interest in connected home electronics but often miss the difference between a useful addition and another device with overlapping functions."
}
